A run of rich text that reads state.

A span is an ordinary node at codegen time, so `passReactivity` sees its props
and writes the updater -- which is the payoff for keeping the family a tree.
On html that has always been free: `md.text(value=string(n))` becomes a
`textContent` write in the handler that moved `n`, and nothing was written for
it.

It is not free everywhere, and this fixture is what says so per target.

  - **html** patches the one text node, which is the whole claim above.
  - **bubbletea** re-renders the view from state on every message, so the
    concatenated flow is rebuilt with the rest of the screen and there is
    nothing to patch.
  - **fyne** has a `*fynetext.Span` in the Model and calls `SetText` on it.
    The span is not a widget, so the setter refreshes the flow that owns it --
    that ownership walk is why a span added to a tree before the tree reaches
    a flow still finds one.
  - **android** re-renders from state like bubbletea, and needs the same
    nothing: `n` is a `mutableStateOf` the composable reads, so the whole
    `buildAnnotatedString` is rebuilt when it moves. That is the payoff for a
    span being a piece of a value rather than a widget -- there is no node to
    find and no setter to write.
  - **gtk4** has no span in the Model at all: a flow is one `GtkLabel` and the
    markup is a Go string expression over the same state the runs were written
    against, so the updater writes the whole label again. The build writes it
    once and the handler writes it again, which the two `LabelSetMarkup` calls
    below are.

deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `LabelSetText` -- a flow's words are markup, and set_text would show the tags rather than obey them
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `Escape\("` -- a literal run is escaped where it is written; a page of prose would otherwise be a page of calls
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `(?m)^\s*(Flow|Span)\(` -- a run that reads state is still no composable; the whole flow is one Text rebuilt from the state it reads
-- doc.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import md "sngl:ui/markup"

output {
    go {
        html
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

ui.window #home(title="doc") {
    var n = 0

    ui.vbox {
        md.paragraph {
            md.text(value="count: ")
            md.bold {
                md.text(value=string(n))
            }
        }
        ui.button(text="+", @click { n += 1 })
    }
}
